\title{Finalization: the machine becomes the default engine, one executable, the notes move into the journal}
\taxon{Session}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{machine}
\tag{soundness}
\tag{platform}
\tag{journal}
\meta{harness}{Claude Code}
\meta{model-id}{claude-fable-5-2}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The last phase of 2026-11-24, from the early evening to about 23:00 local time; in the status logs of the team that is 23:00 UTC on 2026-11-24 to 04:00 UTC on 2026-11-25, and every time of day in the trees of this phase is UTC and marked so. It followed [the exactness reviews](ses-874D), which had left one thing to do: make the machine the default engine under the practical contract. Branch \code{dev}, commits \commit{b869165} to \commit{54bc6c5}; the commit messages name each step. As in the earlier phases the work was done by a team of agents: an integrator of the machine, the owner of the reference engine who also took the loader for this phase, a packaging owner who is the steward of the build, measurement agents, and at the end the agents who moved the documents into this journal.}

\ul{
\li{\strong{The machine's last preconditions.} The hostile suite got the rows of every review, each with the official verdict taken again and its kind: 1,189 rows, later 1,196, 83 of them of the tolerated kind. The one finding of the review that was not a verdict, a decline of valid units by the compiled code, was fixed. The two proof-comparison shortcuts became named switches that bring the switches they need. See [the gate](design-gate) and [the changelog entry of the default set](log-HS1E).}
\li{\strong{The default switch set, by measurement.} The first table on all eight corpora found a cost that three corpora had not shown: with eager reduction, one unit of con-leche ran a probe into the limit of a session. The probes got [a tick budget](log-P6FV). The rule for the choice was refined to the geometric mean of the eight warm passes under a guard of 3 \% per corpus, the congruence segments got [a cap per declaration](log-9636), and a suspected cost of one shortcut turned out to be [the difference between two quiet windows](ins-MBQS). The second table chose the set of wave 6 with eager reduction and both shortcuts: [the decision](dec-YP0N). It supersedes [the set of the wave-6 integration](dec-LZFX) and decides the open half of [the shortcuts as a profile](dec-GL11).}
\li{\strong{The metadata class.} The owner of the reference engine finished the audit of its caches and published the strict mode. A rule of the loader closed the one known file that the practical mode rejected against an official accept, [a node around an application of eagerReduce](log-6K9N). Minutes later the audit built four more through another official test, [finding R2-F4](ex-FD6K), showed that no rule on the position of a node separates them from files that are handled correctly, and the class was closed in the launcher: [a practical rejection of a file with a dropped node is checked again under the strict policy](log-TRJ0). See [the decision](dec-7UAL) and [the caches of the reference engine](design-reference-caches).}
\li{\strong{A latent defect of the level store}, found by a census of universe-level instantiation and fixed in both engines' level module: [the changelog entry](log-XNVE). The memo that the census was for [does not pay](ins-258N).}
\li{\strong{The machine is the default engine} since 03:05 UTC on 2026-11-25, 22:05 local time on 2026-11-24: [the changelog entry](log-65Z0). The evidence was stated before the change and checked after it; it is in [the decision](dec-T79V), step 4, and it closes [the problem](prob-W2FV).}
\li{\strong{Not in the release.} The pooled session arrays with the fix of the young reserve are correct by their gates and [fail the guard](ins-JJ7I) on the new default set. Identity on demand was [not started](dec-36MX). The level memo and the visit filter of evaluation were measured and are not adopted. What stays open is in [one problem tree](prob-HC9J); it also carries the cause of the oversized probe and the evidence behind the tolerated rows.}
\li{\strong{Packaging.} By the maintainer's note of that evening the release is one executable with the fastest default, and a profile-guided build with Oracle GraalVM is an option of the build: [packaging](design-packaging), [the changelog entry](log-Z220). The settings of a plain run were chosen on cold runs of the executable, one scanner thread and another collection policy: [the decision](dec-EGMG), [the changelog entry](log-RCAL). The guard of a distribution runs through the executable in three minutes. The benchmark tables are generated as a tree: [the benchmark tables](rep-benchmarks).}
\li{\strong{The profile-guided build, measured.} [A profile is worth 9 to 12 percent of the image's instructions on Mathlib, and only Oracle GraalVM has it](ins-W0H4); [on Mathlib the JVM launcher needs fewer instructions than every image](ins-8FP8). The full record is [the report](rep-PG1).}
\li{\strong{The repository became public} during this phase, with two workflows on every push: the module tests, and the build of this journal as a web site. The maintainer's notes 14 to 16 of that evening, on the licences, on the notes and on the release, are in [standing policies](standing-policies).}
\li{\strong{The notes move into the journal.} The maintainer's rule of 2026-11-24: every note of the project lives in this forest, and outside it only README files remain. The journal got two kinds for long trees, the [studies](studies) and the [reports](reports), and a procedure for moving a document whole. 59 documents were moved: the research documents, the profiles and reviews, the design documents in full, the working notes of the machine's packages and its list of switches, the notes to the benchmark tables, and the maintainer's notes. An independent pass compared 45 of the moved trees with their documents, 2,017,776 characters, found no text missing and repaired three alterations. Citations of the moved documents in code, READMEs and scripts now carry the address of the tree. The short trees that stated the state of the afternoon were then revised.}
}

\p{\strong{State at the end.} A plain run of the executable is the machine with its default switch set, under the practical policy; the reference engine re-checks every rejection, decides every decline, and alone it is the strict policy. On the frozen set of jars the gate of the default configuration passes through the executable and through the jars: 230 of 230 published tests, 17,775 mutants with no soundness and no completeness difference, the hostile suite of 1,196 rows with no wrong accept and no wrong reject and 68 tolerated accepts. The arena's own procedure on its 270 tests gives no wrong verdict on the final build, see [the report](rep-AR2). Warm, with 8 workers, a pass over Mathlib takes the executable 15.46 s and the JVM launcher 12.44 s, on the aarch64 development host. Nothing was measured on x86-64.}

\p{\strong{Trees of this phase.} New: the decisions [dec-YP0N](dec-YP0N), [dec-7UAL](dec-7UAL) and [dec-EGMG](dec-EGMG); the design note [design-packaging](design-packaging); the changelog entries [log-P6FV](log-P6FV), [log-9636](log-9636), [log-HS1E](log-HS1E), [log-6K9N](log-6K9N), [log-TRJ0](log-TRJ0), [log-65Z0](log-65Z0), [log-Z220](log-Z220), [log-RCAL](log-RCAL) and [log-XNVE](log-XNVE); the example [ex-FD6K](ex-FD6K); the insights [ins-W0H4](ins-W0H4), [ins-8FP8](ins-8FP8), [ins-JJ7I](ins-JJ7I), [ins-MBQS](ins-MBQS) and [ins-258N](ins-258N); the problem [prob-HC9J](prob-HC9J); and the studies and reports. Closed: [prob-W2FV](prob-W2FV) and [prob-8MJ2](prob-8MJ2). Superseded: [dec-LZFX](dec-LZFX) and [dec-WX9Z](dec-WX9Z). Revised to the state of the evening: the index and [accepted risks](accepted-risks); the design notes on [the switches](design-switches), [eager reduction](design-eager-reduction), [the shortcuts](design-proof-comparison-shortcuts), [the divergence classes](design-official-divergence), [the exactness contract](design-exactness-contract), [the gate](design-gate), [the launchers](design-launchers), [the loader](design-export-loader), [conversion](design-conversion), [the reference engine](design-reference-engine), [the machine](design-machine-worklist), [the architecture](design-architecture), [warm sessions](design-warm-sessions), [the measurement method](design-measurement-method) and [the review method](design-adversarial-review); the decisions [dec-T79V](dec-T79V), [dec-GL11](dec-GL11), [dec-X2UF](dec-X2UF), [dec-USLM](dec-USLM), [dec-QN1O](dec-QN1O), [dec-TQSI](dec-TQSI), [dec-6E82](dec-6E82), [dec-OC1F](dec-OC1F), [dec-4TQJ](dec-4TQJ), [dec-36MX](dec-36MX) and [dec-E3EX](dec-E3EX); the problems [prob-TJK3](prob-TJK3), [prob-UN63](prob-UN63), [prob-BIN4](prob-BIN4) and [prob-BHBU](prob-BHBU); and nine insights and two examples that named a switch as off or a number as the latest, each with a paragraph that says what came later.}

\p{\strong{Next.} [Two optimisation waves after the first release, and the level fix](ses-Q8QP).}
